{"type": "complete", "response": "I don\u2019t have the ability to see your screen, so I can\u2019t tell you the title or name of the window that\u2019s currently active.  \n\n**If you\u2019d like to check it yourself:**\n\n- **macOS:** Look at the left side of the menu bar (the app\u2019s icon) or the title bar of the window itself. You can also press **\u2318\u202fTab** to see the list of open apps and which one is active.  \n- **Windows:** The active window\u2019s title appears in the center of the taskbar, and the app\u2019s icon is highlighted on the taskbar. Press **Alt\u202f+\u202fTab** to cycle through open windows and see their titles.  \n- **Linux (most desktop environments):** The title bar of the active window shows its name, and the panel/taskbar usually highlights the active application. You can also use **Alt\u202f+\u202fTab** to view the list.\n\nIf you need help extracting that information programmatically (e.g., via a script), just let me know which operating system you\u2019re on and I can suggest a quick command or snippet.", "session_id": "default", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "model_key": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "model_provider": "omniroute", "model_fallback_used": false, "model_fallback_reason": "", "model_latency_ms": 8328, "model_ttft_ms": 6660, "intent": "conversation", "goal_id": "", "state": "", "executive": {"intent": "conversation", "message": "I don\u2019t have the ability to see your screen, so I can\u2019t tell you the title or name of the window that\u2019s currently active.  \n\n**If you\u2019d like to check it yourself:**\n\n- **macOS:** Look at the left side of the menu bar (the app\u2019s icon) or the title bar of the window itself. You can also press **\u2318\u202fTab** to see the list of open apps and which one is active.  \n- **Windows:** The active window\u2019s title appears in the center of the taskbar, and the app\u2019s icon is highlighted on the taskbar. Press **Alt\u202f+\u202fTab** to cycle through open windows and